    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **The Turn-Up**: Dealer flips a card for trumps. 2. **The Beg**: Non-dealer (Eldest) can either 'Stand' (accept trump) or 'Beg'. 3. **The Gift/Run**: If they beg, dealer can: \n   - 'Gift' 1 point to the opponent and keep the trump suit.\n   - OR 'Run the cards': Deal 3 more cards to each player. Flip a new trump. (If the new suit is the same as the first, keep running 3 at a time until a different suit appears).\n4. **Discarding**: If the cards were run, players discard down to exactly 6 cards before play starts. 5. **Play**: Follow suit or trump. 6. **Scoring**: Points awarded in order: High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    Player: "1. **The Turn-Up**: Dealer flips a card for trumps. 2. **The Beg**: Non-dealer (Eldest) can either 'Stand' (accept trump) or 'Beg'. 3. **The Gift/Run**: If they beg, dealer can: \n   - 'Gift' 1 point to the opponent and keep the trump suit.\n   - OR 'Run the cards': Deal 3 more cards to each player. Flip a new trump. (If the new suit is the same as the first, keep running 3 at a time until a different suit appears).\n4. **Discarding**: If the cards were run, players discard down to exactly 6 cards before play starts. 5. **Play**: Follow suit or trump. 6. **Scoring**: Points awarded in order: High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    objective: 'Score 7 points by winning High, Low, Jack, and Game in several hands.',
    gameplay: "1. **The Turn-Up**: Dealer flips a card for trumps. 2. **The Beg**: Non-dealer (Eldest) can either 'Stand' (accept trump) or 'Beg'. 3. **The Gift/Run**: If they beg, dealer can: \n   - 'Gift' 1 point to the opponent and keep the trump suit.\n   - OR 'Run the cards': Deal 3 more cards to each player. Flip a new trump. (If the new suit is the same as the first, keep running 3 at a time until a different suit appears).\n4. **Discarding**: If the cards were run, players discard down to exactly 6 cards before play starts. 5. **Play**: Follow suit or trump. 6. **Scoring**: Points awarded in order: High, Low, Jack, Game.",
    keyRules: [
      'High (1 pt): Held by the player dealt the highest trump.',
      'Low (1 pt): Held by the player dealt the lowest trump.',
      'Jack (1 pt): Awarded to the team that WINS the trick containing the Jack of trumps.',
      "Game (1 pt): Awarded to the team with the most 'pips' from captured tricks (A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1, 10=10).",
      'Game Tie: If the pip count is tied, the point goes to the non-dealing side (Eldest).',
    ],
